.TH WALLY 1 "2026-11-26" "wally 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wally \- minimal Wayland wallpaper setter with animated GIF and WebP support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wally
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B wally
\fIIMAGE\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B wally
\fBset\fR|\fBquery\fR|\fBrestore\fR|\fBstop\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wally
sets a wallpaper on every output of a compositor that implements
\fBwlr\-layer\-shell\fR (Sway, Hyprland, river, niri, Wayfire, labwc, KDE
Plasma). It is a single self\-contained Rust binary with no runtime library
dependencies: the Wayland client, the image decoders and the compositor are
all pure Rust.
.PP
Still images, animated GIF and animated WebP are supported, as are solid
colours. Animations run at the timing stored in the file and stop consuming
CPU when no output can present them (screen off, session locked, output
occluded). A static wallpaper costs no CPU after its first frame.
.PP
Options apply to every output by default. After
.B \-\-output
they apply only to the named output, until the next
.BR \-\-output .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i ", " \-\-image " " PATH
Image to display. A bare path is accepted as shorthand.
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-color " " COLOR
Solid colour instead of an image, as #RGB or #RRGGBB.
.TP
.BI \-m ", " \-\-mode " " MODE
Scaling mode: \fBstretch\fR, \fBfill\fR (default), \fBfit\fR,
\fBcenter\fR or \fBtile\fR.
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " " NAME
Apply the options that follow to this output only.
.TP
.BI \-b ", " \-\-background " " COLOR
Padding colour for \fBfit\fR and \fBcenter\fR. Default #000000.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-no\-animate
Show only the first frame of an animation.
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " " FACTOR
Animation playback rate between 0.1 and 10. Default 1 (the file's own
timing).
.TP
.BI \-\-transition " " KIND
Animate the first frame with \fBfade\fR or \fBwipe\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-duration " " MS
Transition length in milliseconds. Default 300.
.TP
.B \-\-replace
Take over from a running wally instance after the first frame is on
screen, so changing the wallpaper does not flash black.
.TP
.BI \-\-rotate " " DIR
Foreground\-only rotation: show the images in DIR and advance every
interval. Starts with the first image immediately.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " " DUR
Rotation period: 90s, 30m, 2h, 1h30m. Default 30m.
.TP
.B \-\-shuffle
With \fB\-\-rotate\fR, visit the files in random order. Every file is shown
once per cycle.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Stay resident and serve \fBset\fR, \fBquery\fR, \fBrestore\fR and
\fBstop\fR on a Unix socket in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR.
.TP
.B \-\-scale\-force " " N
Render at this integer buffer scale instead of the output's reported scale.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-outputs
Print each connected output (name, mode, scale, transform) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Validate the images, print the decoded dimensions and the scaling decision
per output, then exit without drawing.
.TP
.B \-\-query
Print the wallpaper last set per output, from the state file.
.TP
.B \-\-restore
Re\-apply the wallpaper last set per output.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine\-readable output for \fB\-\-list\-outputs\fR and \fB\-\-query\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
These talk to a running \fB\-\-daemon\fR instance.
.TP
.B set [OPTIONS]
Apply a new configuration to the running daemon.
.TP
.B query
Print what the daemon is showing.
.TP
.B restore
Re\-apply the last recorded state.
.TP
.B stop
Shut the daemon down.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B fill
Scale to cover the output and crop the overflow (default).
.TP
.B fit
Scale to fit inside the output, letterboxing with the background colour.
.TP
.B stretch
Distort the image to fill the output.
.TP
.B center
Show the image 1:1, centred.
.TP
.B tile
Repeat the image at its original size.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WALLY_DEBUG
Set to 1 to print resident memory and CPU time as they change, 2 to also
trace skipped commits and per\-frame compose rectangles.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Directory for \fBwally/state.conf\fR. Default \fI~/.local/state\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory for the daemon control socket.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The compositor to connect to.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B wally ~/pictures/wall.jpg
Set one image on every output.
.TP
.B wally \-o DP\-1 \-i left.jpg \-o eDP\-1 \-i right.jpg
Different wallpaper per monitor.
.TP
.B wally \-i loop.webp \-\-speed 2
Play an animated WebP at twice its native speed.
.TP
.B wally \-\-rotate ~/pictures/wallpapers \-\-interval 30m \-\-shuffle
Rotate a folder in random order every 30 minutes.
.TP
.B wally \-\-replace \-\-transition fade \-i next.png
Swap the wallpaper without a black gap, fading into the new image.
.TP
.B wally \-\-list\-outputs \-\-json
Print outputs as JSON for a status bar or script.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a runtime error (unreadable image, no compositor,
unsupported protocol), 2 on a usage error.
.SH COMPOSITORS
Requires \fBwlr\-layer\-shell\fR and \fBwl_shm\fR: Sway, Hyprland, river,
niri, Wayfire, labwc and KDE Plasma work. GNOME does not implement layer
shell and is not supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swaybg (1),
.BR sway (1)
.PP
Project home: https://github.com/SONGOKU00mjk/WALLY
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/SONGOKU00mjk/WALLY/issues with the output
of \fBwally \-\-list\-outputs\fR and \fBWALLY_DEBUG=1 wally \-i FILE\fR.
